# Security Policy - False Positive Configuration

# Exclude educational security research materials from secret scanning
wordlists/
payloads/
shells/

# These directories contain EDUCATIONAL SECURITY RESEARCH MATERIALS
# NOT actual secrets or credentials

# Wordlist files contain:
# - DNS enumeration lists
# - Directory enumeration lists  
# - Username/password lists for testing
# - Subdomain lists
# - Fuzzing wordlists

# Payload files contain:
# - SQL injection test vectors
# - XSS test vectors
# - LFI/RFI test payloads
# - Command injection examples
# - XXE/SSRF test cases

# Shell files contain:
# - Educational web shells for security research
# - Post-exploitation examples
# - Penetration testing utilities

# These are LEGITIMATE EDUCATIONAL MATERIALS for:
# - Authorized penetration testing
# - Security research and education
# - Professional cybersecurity training
# - Academic security studies

# Any "secrets" detected in these files are:
# - False positives from pattern matching
# - Educational examples demonstrating vulnerabilities
# - Test data for security assessment tools
# - Research materials for authorized testing

# ONLY scan for actual secrets in:
# - Source code files (*.py)
# - Configuration files (config/)
# - Documentation files
# - Dependency files (requirements.txt)
